# Legacy URLs from the pre-Next static site.
#
# These were `redirects()` in next.config.ts, which static export ignores. Cloudflare
# applies redirects ahead of asset matching, so these win over the built-in .html
# handling and return a proper 301 rather than its 307.
#
# The old config also had a `/:path*.html` catch-all sending everything else to `/`.
# That CANNOT be expressed here: a splat may only appear at the end of the source
# path. Do not try `/:page.html /` as a substitute — Cloudflare splits the source on
# `/` and reads a leading `:` as a whole-segment placeholder, so that rule would match
# `/about` and 301 it to the homepage.
#
# Unmatched legacy .html URLs now return a genuine 404, which Google treats better
# than a blanket redirect to the homepage (it classifies those as soft 404s anyway).
#
# The full list below came from the Wayback Machine's index of the old site
# (web.archive.org/cdx/search/cdx?url=thebluwavegroup.com*&output=text&fl=original),
# which found 14 legacy pages. Every one that has a sensible destination is mapped.
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped, because they were never real pages and have no equivalent:
#   /tooltip_crossbrowser/quote_me.html   a JS tooltip fragment
#   /home_header.htm, /home_main.htm      frameset fragments
# These return a genuine 404, which is the correct answer for a URL that was never
# a destination in the first place.

# Direct equivalents.
/index.html                 /                          301
/about.html                 /about                     301
/contact.html               /contact                   301
/services.html              /services                  301
/free_quotation.html        /quote                     301
/prices_delivery.html       /shipping                  301

# Renamed rather than removed: "creative services" is the design and artwork
# service, and artwork specs are covered in the same place.
/creative_services.html     /services/design-artwork   301
/artwork_specs.html         /services/design-artwork   301

# Reviews and testimonials moved onto the about page.
/customer_comments.html     /about                     301

# The old callback request is now part of the quote form, which offers a call back.
/callback.html              /quote                     301

# The old site had a file-upload page; the new one takes artwork by email off the
# back of an enquiry, so the contact form is the closest real destination.
/sendfiles.html             /contact                   301
/upload.html                /contact                   301

# There is no offers page any more. Products is the nearest useful landing point
# for someone who followed a link about a deal.
/specials.html              /products                  301
